Cobi fork patch 0008: no yadif. VLC's deinterlace filter compiled FFmpeg's yadif line filter from
modules/video_filter/deinterlace/yadif.h, which is GPL-2.0-or-later (Michael Niedermayer); the rest
of the plugin is LGPL. This libVLC ships in App Store apps under the LGPL only, so the yadif and
yadif2x modes go:

- deinterlace/: algo_yadif.c/.h, yadif.h and yadif_x86.asm (the asm is LGPL, but only yadif used
  it) are deleted; Makefile.am and meson.build stop listing them; deinterlace.c drops the two
  modes from its table, deinterlace.h from its option lists.
- The core stops offering the two mode names: src/libvlc-module.c (the deinterlace-mode choices),
  src/video_output/interlacing.c (the modes the vout accepts), lib/video.c
  (libvlc_video_set_deinterlace). Asking for "yadif" now fails there instead of opening a filter
  without it.

The default does not change: "auto" picks "x" (SetFilterMethod in deinterlace.c), as before.
Cobi Player's Scripts/check-engine-gpl-free.sh refuses an engine that names yadif2x.

